/-!
General-field Hecke seven-eighths formalization: verified partial foundations.

Actual continuous unitary characters, finite conductor quotients, infinity
parameters, convergent ideal L-series and all derivatives are constructed.
The series equals its Euler product and is nonzero on Re(s) > 1. Finite
Fourier algebra, local Gauss support, Gaussian Mellin smoothing and smooth
annular truncation estimates are proved on their stated domains.
For universe-zero number fields, actual meromorphic continuation and the
completed functional equation are proved through the audited Tate bridge,
including entire non-norm characters and exact simple poles for pure norm
twists. The actual S-integer orbit count, weighted profile tails and primitive
finite characters for principal S-integer moduli are also proved.
Actual norm-one orbital profiles are smooth in log radius, with their
derivatives given by Euler transforms and controlled by finite original
Schwartz seminorms.
Periodic orbital Poisson retains the actual finite divisor Fourier
coefficients, both orbital zero terms, and all original unit sectors.
The ideal mask is reconstructed by its actual divisor expansion, and the
dual orbital truncation has a uniform power-error bound. Actual compact
two-column annular partition kernels are Schwartz, with polynomial
seminorm costs for their moving archimedean log-norm phase.
Their total-norm Fourier kernels have uniform seminorm bounds over finite
fibres and moving Mellin heights. Product-lattice Poisson retains both axes
and the exact mixed-Haar factor. Actual sextic residue characters and their
S-integer evaluations use the reduction and complex image of one specified
global root, with sixth-power invariance for the original subgroup.
The actual total-norm annular kernel satisfies translated product Poisson
and absolute dual-lattice summation bounds for fixed ideals. Simultaneous
three-index translation preserves the literal frequency ratio and retains
every original subgroup coordinate in the orbit enumeration.

The seven-eighths endpoint remains conditional on explicit analytic inputs.
Literal correlation reconstruction, theta reflection, canonical moments
and arithmetic descent still have unproved obligations. No general seven-eighths
Hecke theorem is asserted by importing this library.
-/
